# UI/UX Refinement & Modernization Plan — CampusFix IT Platform

## Executive Summary

This plan outlines a comprehensive **UI/UX refinement pass** to elevate CampusFix into a modern, enterprise-grade IT incident resolution platform.

The refinement preserves **100% of all existing backend capabilities, OpenRouter / NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Ultra integration, `/api/chat`, and data models** while focusing strictly on:
1. Simplifying IT examples to 1–2 clear universal scenarios (Wi-Fi drop & SSO/2FA login).
2. Redesigning the AI Chatbot into a modern, conversational IT workbench.
3. Fixing all icon/text alignment, padding, and button sizing issues.
4. Restructuring the Technician and Host dashboards for intuitive information hierarchy.
5. Providing a robust, zero-flash Light/Dark theme token system.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - All existing backend routes (`/api/chat`, `/api/health`, `/api/tickets`, `/api/status`, `/api/kb`, `/api/reports`) and data models will remain untouched.
> - Examples on the landing page, chat welcome message, and prompts will be streamlined to 1–2 realistic, universally understood IT issues (e.g., Campus Wi-Fi & SSO login recovery).
> - The Host role remains strictly **read-only**, focused exclusively on executive SLA and incident analytics.

